FROM nginx:alpine
USER appuser
RUN useradd -m appuser
WORKDIR /app
COPY . .
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s \
CMD curl -f http://localhost/ || exit 1
EXPOSE 8080

This was the dockerfile which we had to debug.
In this on line 2 USER has been declared as appuser, but appuser cannot be found as it has not been added so one simple fix is RUN useradd -D appuser should be on line 2 and USER appuser must be on line 3.
Instead of -m we shoule use -D so user is created in default settings.

Corrected dockerfile

FROM nginx:alpine
RUN adduser -D appuser
USER appuser
WORKDIR /app
COPY . .
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s \
CMD curl -f http://localhost/ || exit 1
EXPOSE 8080

